 - `summary`: a single line of at most 120 characters, shown in the agents' ticket list
 - `respond_within_hours`: 72, 24, 8 or 1, depending on the urgency
 
+- `defaulted`: the fields (`queue`, `urgency`, `summary`) the model did not answer usably and that were filled with a default (`general`, `normal`, the subject line)
+- `needs_review`: `True` when `defaulted` is not empty. These tickets never got a real verdict, so a person should open them straight away; a ticket the model really judged `general` / `normal` has `needs_review` `False`.
+
 Anything the model answers outside these lists is replaced by `general` and `normal`. A ticket with neither subject nor body raises `ValueError`.
 
 Run the tests with `python -m unittest` from this directory.
